      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "436dc5bcdff35dbc4243540a75562b817be25c3f",
            "subject": "LU-20690 ec: implement STRIPE I/O scope"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-07 19:44:59.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-07 19:45:12.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20690 tests: read one parity stripe in sanity-ec 312",
        "message": "LU-20690 tests: read one parity stripe in sanity-ec 312\n\nsanity-ec test_312 read the parity mirror of a 4+2 file through the\nMIRROR scope, expecting a buffered read to be refused with -EINVAL\nand a direct read to succeed.  Once \"ec: store EC parity like\nRAID10\" stores every parity slot as p stripes,\nlov_io_designated_stripe_valid() refuses any read of such a slot that\ndoes not name one of its stripes, so the direct read would fail with\n-EINVAL as well, and the buffered read would be refused for that\nreason rather than for being buffered.\n\nRead stripe 0 of the parity slot through the STRIPE scope in both\ncases, which does not depend on how the parity is stored.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec ostcount=8\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I85c401147239ee13b3683b747b0edfdaf13ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
